{
  "_readme": "Captures of the product for the landing (docs/landing-spec.md §6.2), taken by scripts/landing/capture-console.ts from the real console and its BFF served on localhost over a synthetic world (scripts/landing/console-world.ts), always with the neutral brand. Each capture names its route, the state of its world, the language, the viewports, how the picture is framed, the manifest entry it replaces (if any), what it needs to exist in the tree first, and the moment it shows; a `guest-scene` capture also names the scene of the guest template its world jumps to, the last entry of the main story its conversations hold (story-thread.ts, story-evidence.ts, story-mail.ts) and whose phone the simulator shows, and may press a button of the view or put a second view beside the first. The steps to reach each moment live in scripts/landing/scenes.ts. `images` is the ledger the pipeline writes: per capture and viewport, the hash of the picture's pixels and of every file written under packages/web/public, so a run that moves no pixel writes no file. Synthetic data only, no real person, never taken in CI, with credentials or against a deployed stage.",
